  { icon: '🚶', title: 'Don\'t Say "British Isles"', text: 'Ireland is not part of the UK and the term "British Isles" is politically sensitive. Say "Ireland and Britain" instead. Also, it\'s "Republic of Ireland" or just "Ireland" — never "Southern Ireland".' },
  { icon: '🎵', title: 'Trad Sessions', text: 'If you find a trad music session in a pub, sit quietly and listen. Don\'t talk loudly over the music, clap between tunes (not during), and never request "Danny Boy" — it\'s a tourist cliche.' },
  { icon: '💚', title: 'GAA & Sports', text: 'Gaelic football and hurling are Ireland\'s national sports — catch a game at Croke Park if you can. Asking about someone\'s county team is an instant conversation starter in any pub.' },
];
